    "summary": "Dark Star suite shines, tight jams and soaring Saint Stephen",
    "blurb": "The second set launches into a blazing Dark Star/Attics of My Life/Sugar Magnolia arc that flows into a classic Saint Stephen > China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider sequence. Jerry’s lead guitar is on fire, Phil lays down a deep, supportive bass foundation, and the dual drummers keep the energy relentless. Highlights also include the heartfelt Swing Low encore and the crisp Not Fade Away → Easy Wind transition.",
    "review": "Port Chester’s June 24‑1970 show captures the Dead at a creative peak. After an acoustic first set that sets a relaxed tone, the band erupts on the late electric half with a near‑perfect Dark Star suite – the opening sustained bass note, Garcia’s smoking leads and Pigpen’s subtle textures create a trance‑like groove that flows seamlessly into Attics of My Life and then bursts out into an early version of Sugar Magnolia. The momentum carries through Not Fade Away → Easy Wind and builds to a climactic Saint Stephen > China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, where Jerry’s soaring solos and Bob’s rhythmic weave lock in with Mickey’s gong intro and Bill’s driving tom‑tom feel. The encore closes the night on an emotional note with Swing Low (Sweet Chariot), leaving fans with both high‑energy fireworks and a lingering sense of intimacy.",
